# NestedText v3 - tei/ per-module DETAIL pass (measured 2026-09-16)
# Source: cc-resources/.dtd-file-examples/tei/ (20 name.dtd, script census).
# Fourth of the what-is-not-yet-transmigrated remainder: tei 20 modules.

module-census:
    core: 83 elements, header 69, msdescription 69, namesdates 56, tagdocs 54
    textstructure 33, dictionaries 33, transcr 30, iso-fs 28, drama 17
    corpus 14, spoken 14, textcrit 14, nets 12, analysis 11, gaiji 11, linking 11
    figures 7, verse 4, certainty 3
    total: 573 elements across 20 modules

one-to-one-measured:
    > Every module declares exactly as many entities as elements: 83/83,
    > 69/69, 3/3, without exception across all twenty. Each element rides
    > with its classes and hooks in the same file, so a module is
    > removable whole: delete the file and its elements vanish with their
    > machinery, never orphaned. Modularity as an arithmetic invariant.

size-bands:
    > Above 30 KB: core header msdescription. 10-30 KB: namesdates tagdocs
    > textstructure dictionaries transcr iso-fs. Below 10 KB: the other
    > eleven, verse and certainty under 5 KB. A module earns its file by
    > cohesion, never by size: certainty's 3 elements still ship alone.

release-binding:
    > Stream 19 (convergence): the 1:1 invariant is the removability test
    > every converged subset must pass; a subset whose elements outlive
    > their file is not converged. Stream 9 (triple): twenty modules one
    > ODD source stays the generation precedent beside lwdita's conductor.
